{
  "dom_id": "step-q328369",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x+{45}^{\u2218})=1,$ for $-{180}^{\u2218}\\le x<0,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{45}^{\u2218} & ={45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-{45}^{\u2218}+{45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-{180}^{\u2218}\\le x<0.$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=-{180}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-{90}^{\u2218}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-{180}^{\u2218}\\le x<0.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={-180}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{2}={-90}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
